<span style="color:lightyellow"><span id="response">You were brought up as a devoted Christian. This also meant that your parents shielded you from all sin, and homeschooled you most of your life. When you reached the age to enter highschool, your parents knew they had to let go, at least of some of the things they shielded you from. Your time in high school was... Strange. Boys. Girls. Bullying. Sexual harrassment. It was a whole deal. With it being over, you were ready to embark on a journey to figure out who you were. Until...</span></span>
<<done>>
	<<script>>
		$("#radiobutton-upbring-0").on("click", function (event) {
			$("#response").text("You were brought up as a devoted Christian. This also meant that your parents shielded you from all sin, and homeschooled you most of your life. When you reached the age to enter highschool, your parents knew they had to let go, at least of some of the things they shielded you from. Your time in high school was... Strange. Boys. Girls. Bullying. Sexual harrassment. It was a whole deal. With it being over, you were ready to embark on a journey to figure out who you were. Until...");
		});
		$("#radiobutton-upbring-1").on("click", function (event) {
			$("#response").text("You were brought up as an active kid. Football, hockey. Your parents seemed to think that having done a lot of sport as a child would make you a more complete adult. Your body has changed significantly because of it. A toned body with muscles, a great ass, a beautiful chest. Your friends were jealous, even though they kept telling you they were not. You never drank, you never did drugs. You focused most of your life on sports and activities.");
		});
		$("#radiobutton-upbring-2").on("click", function (event) {
			$("#response").text("Your parents were rarely around. Your mother always working, and your father always absent. You were left to be raised on your own. You turned into a brat in no time, and your parents didn't know how to deal with that. They still loved you, though. What else were they supposed to do? You didn't follow much in school, and didn't have 'good' friends. For some reason, you still got good grades. Call it luck.");
		});
        $("#radiobutton-upbring-3").on("click", function (event) {
			$("#response").text("Your parents did what they could to shield you from the horrible truth of the world, and of what the human mind is capable of doing. This has made you extremely gullible, and you're no longer quite sure whether someone is being sarcastic or not. This has also turned you into quite the airhead. As an effect, your inhibition is... not what it should be. To you, nothing seems off anyways. It has always been this way.");
		});
        $("#radiobutton-upbring-5").on("click", function (event) {
			$("#response").text("You were raised as a bookworm. Always reading something. This has made you insanely good in school. Always a grade A student, not matter the subject. Maths? Easy. Biology? Easy. People always wanted to be with you in group assignments. It didn't take long for you to realise that it wasn't because they liked you, but only because you were a nerd. Good at school. It hurts. But you didn't care. It was human interaction. Somebody to talk to, even if it was just school stuff.");
		});

        $(document).on("click", "#upbring1", function (event) {
			$("#response").text("Your parents has always given you exactly what you were pointing at, at all times in your life. Smothered you with love and given you zero repurcussions to anything you did. You seek attention, actually almost willing to whore yourself out to get it. Anything for a compliment, anything for a human interaction. You can be really clingly at times. Well, most times. In school, you were well-liked. Perhaps because you talked with anyone at any time.");
		});
        $(document).on("click", "#upbring2", function (event) {
			$("#response").text("You were raised to be loud. To be 'heard'. No matter if people wanted to hear you or not. You didn't care if you were being rude or not, as long as people heard what you had to say. Even if it was stupid. Being obnoxious was almost part of your personality. It was who you were. To your friends, family and strangers. Deep inside, you knew this was wrong. You knew this was not what you wanted. But it was who you were. Who you are.");
		});
	<</script>>
<</done>>
